This is the right approach. Locking down the end-to-end flow for Manual Entry ensures our state machine, routing, and edge cases are rock-solid before we introduce the massive volume and parallel processing complexities of Bulk Upload.
To finish the manual flow, we need to implement the final three pieces:
 1. **The Background Scheduler** (to automatically post delayed batches).
 2. **Role-Based Dashboard Fetching** (so approvers only see batches assigned to their step).
 3. **Maker Cancellation** (enforcing the rule that batches can only be deleted at PENDING_L1).
Here is the code to complete the end-to-end manual flow.
### Step 1: The Background Execution Scheduler
When a final approver schedules a batch for the future, its status becomes SCHEDULED. We need a Cron job that wakes up every minute, finds due batches, and executes them.
**1. Create a New File:** VoucherExecutionScheduler.java (in com.fincore.VoucherService.Service)
```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.Service;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.VoucherPosting;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Models.enums.RequestStatus;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Dto.BulkProcessVoucherPostingDto;
import com.fincore.VoucherService.Repository.VoucherPostingRepository;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.springframework.data.redis.core.StringRedisTemplate;
import org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Scheduled;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;

import java.time.LocalDateTime;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class VoucherExecutionScheduler {

    private final VoucherPostingRepository voucherPostingRepository;
    private final VoucherRequestServiceImpl voucherRequestService;
    private final StringRedisTemplate stringRedisTemplate;

    /**
     * Runs every 60 seconds. Uses a Redis lock to ensure only one pod 
     * executes the scheduled batches in a distributed environment.
     */
    @Scheduled(fixedRate = 60000)
    @Transactional
    public void executeScheduledBatches() {
        String lockKey = "SYSTEM_LOCK_SCHEDULED_EXECUTION";
        boolean lockAcquired = false;

        try {
            Boolean acquired = stringRedisTemplate.opsForValue()
                    .setIfAbsent(lockKey, "LOCKED", 2, TimeUnit.MINUTES);
            lockAcquired = Boolean.TRUE.equals(acquired);

            if (!lockAcquired) return;

            // Find all SCHEDULED batches where the time is <= NOW
            List<VoucherPosting> dueBatches = voucherPostingRepository.findAll().stream()
                    .filter(p -> "SCHEDULED".equals(p.getCurrentStatus()) 
                            && p.getScheduledTime() != null 
                            && !p.getScheduledTime().isAfter(LocalDateTime.now()))
                    .collect(Collectors.toList());

            if (dueBatches.isEmpty()) return;

            log.info("SCHEDULER_WAKEUP | Found {} batches ready for execution.", dueBatches.size());

            for (VoucherPosting posting : dueBatches) {
                try {
                    // Update State
                    posting.setCurrentStatus("POSTED");
                    posting.setExecutedAt(LocalDateTime.now());
                    voucherPostingRepository.save(posting);

                    // Execute Oracle Logic via existing pipeline
                    // Using "SYSTEM" as the executor ID since it's automated
                    BulkProcessVoucherPostingDto execDto = new BulkProcessVoucherPostingDto();
                    execDto.setBatchId(posting.getBatchId());
                    execDto.setStatus(RequestStatus.ACCEPTED);
                    execDto.setRemarks("Executed by System Scheduler");
                    
                    voucherRequestService.processBulkRequestsAsync(execDto, "SYSTEM", 0);
                    
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    log.error("SCHEDULER_FAIL | Batch: {} | Error: {}", posting.getBatchId(), e.getMessage());
                }
            }

        } finally {
            if (lockAcquired) {
                stringRedisTemplate.delete(lockKey);
            }
        }
    }
}

```
