### Step 3: Enforcing Maker Cancellation Rules
The rule states a Maker can cancel their batch **only before any Approver accepts/rejects**. This means the batch must still be at PENDING_L1.
**1. Update VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java:**
Modify the cancelMyRequestsByBatchIdAsync method to include the strict workflow state check.
```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public void cancelMyRequestsByBatchIdAsync(String batchId, String userId) {
        
        // 1. Fetch the workflow state
        VoucherPosting posting = voucherPostingRepository.findById(batchId)
                .orElseThrow(() -> new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Batch not found."));
                
        // 2. Strict Business Rule: Can only delete if NO approver has acted yet (Still L1)
        if (!"PENDING_L1".equals(posting.getCurrentStatus())) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException(
                "Cannot cancel batch. It has already moved to workflow stage: " + posting.getCurrentStatus());
        }

        // 3. Prevent unauthorized deletion
        if (!posting.getCreatedBy().equalsIgnoreCase(userId)) {
            throw new CustomExceptions.InvalidDataException("Security Violation: You can only cancel batches you created.");
        }

        // 4. Lock the legacy master table
        int updated = jdbcTemplate.update(
            "UPDATE JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER SET BATCH_STATUS = 'QUEUED' WHERE BATCH_ID = ? AND CREATOR_ID = ?", 
            batchId, userId);
            
        if (updated == 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Batch already being processed.");
        }

        // 5. Fire off the async deletion (which triggers the PURGE_JOURNAL_BATCH Oracle procedure)
        progressService.sendProgress(batchId, userId, 0, "PROCESSING", "Purging Batch Data...");
        
        // Clean up our new workflow tracking tables synchronously before background purge
        voucherWorkflowRepository.deleteAll(voucherWorkflowRepository.findByBatchIdFkOrderByLastActionAtAsc(batchId));
        voucherPostingRepository.delete(posting);
        
        self.executeAsyncBatchCancellation(batchId, userId);
    }

